# Sub-tick interpolation of the additive tracer ribbon
# (scripts/check_feeder_subtick.sh --path tracer).
#   <bk2> | <V> | blob=<x>,<y> ... [tol=<px>] [step=<px>] [astep=<px>] [cstep=<n>]
#
# The two legs are a render-path selection with and without the tracer path,
# terrain and moby in both.
#
# The source is not a movie: the plain boot's attract demo charges through
# Sunrise Spring, two live ribbon records drawing 18 segments per tick. A tick
# spans VBLs 4499-4500 and 4501-4502 here, so V is 4501 and the intermediate
# present at 4502 covers [4499, 4501]; at V=4500 the present at 4501 falls in
# the next tick and every intermediate leg reads the next tick's ribbon. The
# charge ribbon is one 2818-3192 px component whose head crosses 20.8 px over
# the interval while its tail grows, so all three cells carry signal: the
# centroid is the head's translation, the area the ribbon's own length ramp,
# the mean colour its additive fade. The second record's ribbon, the 436-453 px
# streak at (129.4,78.8), is not named: its head runs off the top of the frame
# and terrain covers its lower half, so its visible centroid is not the lerp
# of its two canonical ones.
title-demo | 4501 | blob=305.3,196.0 tol=1.0 step=10
